  "implementation": [
    "Same finite legacy SourceLoginJsExtensions java host calls source.browser awaited packet under same original RuntimeTask/source owner. Presentation ACK alone is never await success.",
    "refetchAfterSuccess default true: actual page confirmation and checked Cookie capture/dismissal return a confirmation only; original JVM then reparses original URL with initial header snapshot through original AnalyzeUrl/HTTP/Cookie owner on same task, returning original initial analyzed URL.",
    "explicit false: one actual WK JavaScript snapshot carries current URL and DOM HTML together; off-main decode and bounded result pass to the same task.",
    "Owner result uses original synthetic raw200/OK/HTTP1.1/empty response headers. Empty response/user cancellation/task cancellation fail with accepted side effects retained.",
    "One Presenter queue and existing browser/Cookie owner. UIKit actual completion and actual dismissal plus Coordinator Cookie/DOM/initial-seed callback drain own success/cancel receipts; no Host callback reentry into locked source service/JVM.",
    "Finite page-authored close message and real WKUIDelegate webViewDidClose use same mounted confirmation and challenge suppression; ordinary didFinish never substitutes for terminal confirmation.",
    "Initial native Cookie seed callbacks are generation/token guarded and drained after cancellation, including reload predecessors, before an old URL/header may ever load. Nonawait accepted pages still survive normal producer cleanup.",
    "Native authored one method uses sole product process/JNI/default Presenter, real loopback peer and mounted page-close/actual dismiss, second real taskcancel, plus actual WK Cookie callback held across cancel/drain. It has NOT executed."
